{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Maintain the 24-month criminal record buffer for Indefinite Leave to Remain  ",
        "additional_details": "We believe the \"Earned Settlement\" rules permanently deny ILR to long-term UK residents over minor, historic, or non-custodial infractions. In our view, this provides no path to rehabilitation, punishing individuals indefinitely for minor mistakes. We feel the previous 24-month buffer struck a fair balance: it maintained public safety while recognizing minor errors do not make a person permanently unfit for settlement. We believe denying ILR for life over minor offenses is disproportionate, tears families apart, and ignores justice.",
        "background": "Don\u2019t bring in the \"spotless criminal record\" rule for Earned Settlement/ILR. Restore previous suitability rules allowing those with minor, non-custodial offenses to settle after 24 months.",
